<title>BULGARIA: Yield keeps rising on Bulgaria 4-wk T-bills.</title>
<headline>Yield keeps rising on Bulgaria 4-wk T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yield rose further on Bulgaria's Finance Ministry four-week discount T-bills at the daily auction on Thursday as the issue was undersubscribed, central bank figures show.</p>
<p>The average yield to maturity on the issue was 3.81 percent, up from 3.80 percent at Wednesday's auction and 3.78 percent on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Details of the issue follow. Prices in percent of par:</p>
<p> Issue number		  BG3036697004</p>
<p> Maturity			four weeks</p>
<p> Par value		     26,000 million levs</p>
<p> Issue date		    May 30</p>
<p> Maturity date		 June 27</p>
<p> Bids received		 20,016.9 million levs</p>
<p> Avg price of bids	   96.33 pct</p>
<p> Bids approved		 20,016.9 million levs</p>
<p> Avg accepted price	  96.33 pct</p>
<p> Avg yield to maturity     3.81 pct</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 91188</p>
